counterfactuals.output:
1. A solenoid actuator comprising:

an electromagnetic coil configured to receive electrical energy and generate a magnetic field;

a movable armature arranged relative to the electromagnetic coil such that the magnetic field causes movement of the movable armature to convert the electrical energy into mechanical motion;

a drive circuit configured to supply current to the electromagnetic coil; and

a controller operatively coupled to the drive circuit, the controller being configured to:

determine a plurality of current values associated with current supplied to the electromagnetic coil during an energization interval;

determine a duration associated with at least a portion of the energization interval;

form an evaluation product based on the plurality of current values and the duration; and

compare the evaluation product with a threshold to determine an operating condition of the solenoid actuator.
